From cad2ab161b2c2cc938589f0eff5bcb7e02e37a33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:17:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XD Netplay v1.7.3: spectators play a small reserve behind the
 match instead of stuttering

A spectator gets every player's pad entries through the host's relay, one
hop more than the pad buffer is sized for, so its queues kept running dry
and the view stalled in short bursts. A client that owns no pad and no Wii
remote in fixed-delay mode now lets each pad's queue fill to a reserve
(its own ping to the host in entries plus a margin, 24-120) before popping,
and on an underflow raises the reserve a step and refills once. Same
entries, same order; players and host input authority are unchanged. Each
set or raise is logged as a specbuf line.
